

-> @RestController vs @Controller
    @RestController
    public class UserController {
    }

    | @Controller         | @RestController   |
    | ------------------- | ----------------- |
    | Returns View (HTML) | Returns JSON      |
    | Used in MVC apps    | Used in REST APIs |
    | Needs @ResponseBody | Already included  |


-> @RequestMapping & shortcut annotations
    @RequestMapping("/users")

    @GetMapping
    @PostMapping
    @PutMapping
    @DeleteMapping

    Cleaner
    Preferred in real projects

-> Request mapping using HTTP methods
    @GetMapping("/users")
    @PostMapping("/users")
    @PutMapping("/users/{id}")
    @DeleteMapping("/users/{id}")
📌 REST APIs depend on HTTP verbs, not method names.

-> PathVariable vs RequestParam

    @GetMapping("/users/{id}")
    public User getUser(@PathVariable Long id)

    @GetMapping("/users")
    public User getUser(@RequestParam Long id)

    | PathVariable         | RequestParam      |
    | -------------------- | ----------------- |
    | Part of URL          | Query parameter   |
    | Mandatory            | Optional possible |
    | Used for resource ID | Used for filters  |



